<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>local.ianitor</string>

  <!-- Lar Ianitor daemon (see streambinder/lar). Runs at login and
       restarts on crash. Replaces the terminal runs from
       ~/Workspace/code/lar with IANITOR_API_URL exported by hand.

       SETUP on peregrine, in order:
         1. Stop the terminal daemon first, or the two fight over
            port 8717 and the launchd one restarts forever.
         2. Move the models into the default data dir, so the
            daemon needs no IANITOR_MODEL_DIR:
              mkdir -p ~/Library/Application\ Support/Ianitor/models
              mv ~/Workspace/code/lar/models/* \
                 ~/Library/Application\ Support/Ianitor/models/
            The live enrollment already sits in that data dir
            (agent.key, ianitor.redb, logs, frames), so identity,
            store, logs and frame cache need no migration.
         3. Install the binary on PATH (the plist runs `ianitor`,
            resolved through the PATH .shrc sets):
              cp ~/Workspace/code/lar/target/release/ianitor \
                 ~/.local/bin/ianitor
            Re-copy it after every rebuild.
         4. Add this file to the clavis repo as
            Library/LaunchAgents/local.ianitor.plist##os.Darwin,
            commit, push, then yadm pull on this machine.
         5. Load it (the repo bootstrap script does the same
            bootout-then-bootstrap loop for every agent):
              launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) \
                ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.ianitor.plist
       Check: curl -s 127.0.0.1:8717/status

       The daemon gets its two non-default variables from ~/.shrc,
       sourced before exec, so the terminal runs and the daemon
       share one definition and this plist sets no environment:
         IANITOR_API_URL        The code default is
                                http://localhost:8000 (mlx-serve).
                                Release builds bake the production
                                URL in, but a local cargo build has
                                it only when the variable was set at
                                build time. Set it in .shrc and the
                                doubt disappears.
         IANITOR_CAPTURE_CACHE  Off by default; 1 keeps the 60 s
                                frame cache under the data dir.
       launchd expands neither ~ nor $HOME, hence the absolute
       paths below. The shell sources .shrc with $HOME, which
       launchd sets for user agents.

       TCC: the Screen Recording and Automation grants given to
       Ghostty do NOT transfer. The first launchd run prompts
       again, now bound to the ianitor binary in ~/.local/bin.
       Grant both, or capture and the Chrome incognito sensor
       stay blind. A rebuild replaces the binary and may prompt
       again; the .app bundle question is still open.
       -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>. "$HOME/.shrc"; exec ianitor run</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/dpucci/Library/Logs/ianitor.stdout.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/dpucci/Library/Logs/ianitor.stderr.log</string>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
